# This is the processing directive for uni-temporal Anchor Modeling in Snowflake
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
# Snowflake_uni.legacy.directive is the previous version of this list, in the original dialect. The
# golden files in sisula/examples/anchor-snowflake come from it.
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Snowflake/NamingConvention.js
SQL/Snowflake/derive.js
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateEquivalentAndDefault.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateTies.sisula
# to be done later
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateKnotEquivalenceViews.sisula
SQL/Snowflake/uni/CreateAttributeEquivalenceViews.sisula
